# Content files are compared by GIT BLOB SHA — the app's pack updater asks GitHub for a tree listing
# and decides "did this file change?" from the SHA alone, without downloading anything
# (charnik · docs/PLAN.md · REL-4). That only works while the bytes in the blob are the bytes on
# disk, so nothing here may be EOL-translated on the way in or out: with `core.autocrlf=true` a
# Windows checkout rewrites every LF to CRLF, and then every file looks permanently changed to every
# Windows user — a phantom update no one can ever clear.
#
# The converters write LF and no BOM on purpose (`tools/srd/lib.mjs`); CRLF+BOM is for the CSVs the
# app itself writes back, which are a different thing and live in the user's data folder.
